  <h2>We respect your privacy</h2>
  <p>Katrina Ridout Nutrition Pty Ltd ("we", "us") respects your right to privacy and is committed to safeguarding the personal information of our clients and website visitors. We follow the Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth). This policy sets out how we collect, use, disclose and protect personal information. "Personal information" is information we hold that identifies you or could reasonably identify you.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect personal information you give us through our website, by email, by phone, in a consultation or in another form. This can include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, phone number, address and email address</li>
    <li>information you give when you book, enquire, download a guide or sign up to emails</li>
    <li>health and dietary information you share so Kat can provide dietetic care</li>
    <li>payment details needed to process a booking or purchase</li>
    <li>any other information you choose to provide while dealing with us</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Health information is sensitive information under the Privacy Act. We collect it only with your consent and only where it is needed to provide your care.</p>

  <h2>How we collect it</h2>
  <p>We collect personal information when you interact with us online, by phone, by email or in person, when you use our website and when we provide services to you. We may also receive personal information about you from a third party, such as a referring GP or specialist. When we do, we protect it as set out in this policy.</p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>We use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>provide dietetic consultations, written plans and follow-up care</li>
    <li>manage bookings, payments, Medicare and private health claims</li>
    <li>respond to your enquiries and send you information you have asked for</li>
    <li>let you know about services, resources and updates that may be relevant to you, where you have agreed to receive them</li>
    <li>improve our services and understand what our clients need</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may contact you by phone, email, SMS or post. You can opt out of marketing emails at any time using the unsubscribe link in any email, or by emailing us.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We only share personal information where it is needed to deliver our services or where the law requires it. This can include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your GP, specialist or other treating practitioners, with your consent</li>
    <li>service providers that help us run the practice, such as clinical software, booking, payment and email platforms</li>
    <li>our professional advisers and insurers, where reasonably necessary</li>
    <li>government bodies, courts or law enforcement where a law, regulation, court order or legal process requires it</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some of the service providers we use store or process information outside Australia. Where that happens we take reasonable steps to make sure your information is handled in line with the Australian Privacy Principles.</p>
  <p>If there is a change of ownership of the practice, client records may be transferred to the new owner to the extent permitted by law, on condition that they are kept confidential and handled under this policy.</p>

  <h2>How we keep it secure</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, interference, loss and unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Clinical records are kept in secure practice-management software with access controls. Information sent over the internet carries some risk, and we cannot guarantee the security of information you send to us or receive from us by email.</p>

  <h2>Access and correction</h2>
  <p>You can ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct information that is inaccurate, out of date, incomplete or misleading. Email <a href="mailto:info@katridout.com.au">info@katridout.com.au</a>. We will respond within a reasonable time. In some circumstances set out in the Privacy Act we may refuse access, and if so we will tell you why. A small administrative fee may apply to providing copies of records.</p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>If you have a concern about how we have handled your personal information, email Kat Ridout at <a href="mailto:info@katridout.com.au">info@katridout.com.au</a> with the details. We take complaints seriously and will respond promptly after receiving written notice. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.</p>

  <h2>Website and cookies</h2>
  <p>When you visit katridout.com.au we may collect information such as your browser type, operating system, the pages you view and the site you came from. This is used in aggregate to understand how people use the site and to improve it.</p>
  <p>Our website uses cookies. Cookies are small files a website stores in your browser to recognise you when you return and to remember details about your visit. Most browsers accept cookies automatically; you can reject them in your browser settings, though some parts of the site may not work as well.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> sets cookies to measure how visitors use the site. The data is aggregated and does not identify you to us.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Ads</strong> sets cookies so we can measure whether our advertising leads to bookings and enquiries, and may show you relevant ads on Google and other websites.</li>
    <li><strong>Brevo</strong> is the platform we use to send emails you have signed up for. It records whether emails are opened and which links are clicked so we can send you more relevant information.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Our site links to other websites we do not own or control, including the booking page and clinic websites. Those links are for your convenience and do not mean we endorse those sites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, so please read their privacy statements before giving them personal information.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes take effect when the updated policy is published on this page. Please check back occasionally.</p>

